---
id: org.dxos.ui.react-ui-canvas.2d
name: SceneEditor2D
version: 0.1.0
---

The 2D variant of the scene editor: what `SceneEditor` does when its dimension config is `createConfig2D`
(`config2d` with the default node types). The core spec states everything both dimensions share; this spec states
only what 2D adds or does differently — the viewport, its tools and geometry, the grid, lattice and guides, ports and
links, portals, the 2D Properties form and 2D styles.

The 2D viewport (`Viewport2D`) is react-ui-canvas's own engine, the `Canvas`: an infinite, multi-depth diagram
surface where a View is typed nodes and typed links in one flat coordinate space and a node of type `view` opens onto
another View, which is what depth means. The engine keeps its View model as an in-memory working form: the viewport
reads the open scene's 2D layouts into Views (`toCanvasViews`), the engine keeps a gesture's in-flight state in
memory and writes its store once on release, and that one write reaches the editor as one `LayoutIntent` per
changed layout (`viewWrites`) — plus a `ModelIntent` defining the object a new portal or instance places — so the
editor records, undoes and shares 2D edits as it does 3D ones. Nothing stores the View model; the document is the
scene model alone. Selection, tool, drill path, camera and display are the editor's, mirrored into the engine's
atoms both ways.

The engine also runs on its own, outside the editor: a legacy canvas article and plugin-conductor's compute board
render `Canvas` with its own toolbar, history and clipboard. Requirements F-1 to F-9 are the engine's and hold in
both settings; where the editor replaces an engine behaviour, [F-10] says so.

The seam that lets one engine serve every host is the **projection** (decision 11): the surface reads a positioned
`View` and emits `Intent`s, and never writes a coordinate itself. A projection may apply, rewrite or reject each
intent and then re-emits the View. Freehand is the identity projection; constrained, dynamic and compute projections
own a model of their own and position the View from it. `docs/DESIGN.md` carries the engine's reasoning and the
numbered decisions it cites, `docs/VIEWS.md` the reasoning behind Views, Objects and Tags.

Requirements marked **(planned)** are designed and not built.

## Dependencies

```mdl
uses org.dxos.ui.react-ui-canvas: The shared scene editor this variant configures — its parts, store, commands, history, clipboard, lock, roles, panels, inspectors and timeline hold in 2D and are not restated.
```

```mdl
uses org.dxos.scene: The data the 2D viewport reads and writes — `Layout2D`, `Element2D`, `Style2D` and the composite transform.
```

## Ontology

The engine has three concepts: the **View** and the **Object** (containers) and the **Tag**. Drawing order is the
container tree. The word _scene_ means the drawn world (the scene layer, scene coordinates) or the scene model's
`Scene`, never an engine container.

| Term          | Definition                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Canvas**    | The surface. It shows one **root View** and navigates down from it; the navigation path always starts at the root.                                                                                                 |
| **Node**      | A positioned element: a centre, a size, a type and a style. Every node lives in exactly one container.                                                                                                             |
| **Link**      | A connection between two endpoints, each a node (and optional port) or a free point. A link lives in the container of its endpoints, not under its source node, since a link's source can change.                  |
| **Container** | Anything that holds an ordered list of nodes and links: a View or an Object definition.                                                                                                                            |
| **View**      | A `view` node and the contents record it opens: nodes and links with a layout. Drilling into a View makes it the canvas's current View. The root View is the one View no node contains.                            |
| **Object**    | A reusable container definition (`ViewKind` `composite`), drawn wherever it is placed. An Object is not drilled into: it opens in **isolation** to edit its definition, and every placement redraws.              |
| **Instance**  | A node that places an Object: the Object's contents scaled into the instance's box (`fit`), with per-instance `overrides`.                                                                                         |
| **Group**     | What the Group command makes: an **anonymous Object** and one Instance of it in place of the selection. It joins the Objects library when it is **named** or **placed a second time**.                             |
| **Tag**       | A label on any node, link, Instance or Object, many per element. A tag hides, locks or sets the opacity of everything it labels. It has no effect on drawing order. **(planned)**; until then, `Layer` does this. |
| **Order**     | A container's children are an ordered list, drawn first at the back. Moving an element in the Views tree restacks it.                                                                                              |

```
Canvas   ─ shows ─▶ root View
View     ─ contains (ordered) ─▶ Node | Link | View | Instance
Object   ─ contains (ordered) ─▶ Node | Link | Instance          (no View inside an Object)
Instance ─ places ─▶ Object
Tag      ─ labels ─▶ Node | Link | Instance | Object             (many to many)
```

Each engine concept is a part of the scene model, which is what is stored:

| Engine         | Scene model (`org.dxos.scene`)                                                                                   |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Root View      | The open `Scene`'s `Layout2D`.                                                                                    |
| `view` node    | An `Element2D` placing the composite object `view:<layout>`, whose parts are that View's layout.                 |
| Object         | A `Layout2D` with `kind: composite` (`anonymous` when Group made it), the parts of a model object.               |
| Instance       | An `Element2D` placing the object `instance:<composite>`, with the composite transform (`scale`, `fit`).         |
| Node, Link     | An `Element2D`; a link is one with `source` and `target` endpoints. Fields the base lacks live in `props.canvas`. |
| Layer          | An entry of `Layout2D.layers`; `node.layer` is the element's `layer`.                                            |
| Style class    | A named style of the root model (`NamedStyle2D`); a node's `class` is the element's `style`, its `style` the element's `overrides`. |

